---
description: USE WHEN writing styling for shared UI components in the packages/ui directory to prevent global leakage.
globs: ["packages/ui/src/**/*.module.scss"]
alwaysApply: false
---
SCSS Module BEM Standards
1. Naming Convention
Structure: Use strict BEM syntax (.block__element--modifier) even within local SCSS modules.

Purpose: This ensures clear semantic intent and makes it easy to transition styles between components if needed.

2. Scoping & Nesting
Specificity: Limit nesting depth to a maximum of 3 levels. High specificity is an anti-pattern in the ReadBoot system.

Global Escaping: Use :global() sparingly and only for integrating with 3rd-party libraries (e.g., nuqs or Storybook wrappers).

3. Variable Usage
Strict Sourcing:
- Do not hardcode visual values directly in component modules (especially HEX colors and one-off spacing/radius/border numbers).
- `@use` token modules from `packages/ui/src/tokens/**` (legacy: `patterns/Atoms/**` until migration ends). See **`readboot-scss-architecture.mdc`**.
- Pixel primitives are allowed only in token-definition layers (e.g., reference tokens/mixins), not as arbitrary literals in component styles.
